        <fig id="article-24693.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Mallory-Weiss Syndrome on Esophagoscopy.&#x000a0;This image, captured via esophagoscopy, shows the distal esophagus. The visible tissue is ulcerated and torn. This finding is consistent with Mallory-Weiss Syndrome, which is characterized by tears in the esophageal lining caused by forceful vomiting or retching. Shi S-S et al 2023.Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)..</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Capture__dxxcran__2025-08-31__052959" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-24693.s16">
        <fig id="article-24693.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Endoscopic View of Hemoclip Application for Bleeding Control. This endoscopic image shows a medical procedure in progress. A hemoclip has been precisely applied to an area of tissue that appears to be actively bleeding or at risk of bleeding. The clip is deployed to achieve hemostasis. This intervention is commonly used to stop gastrointestinal bleeding. Shi S-S, et al 2023.Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Capture__dxxcran__2025-08-31__053047" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-24693.s17">
        <fig id="article-24693.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Diagnostic and Therapeutic Algorithm for Mallory-Weiss Syndrome. This flowchart outlines the clinical management of hematemesis or melena. The initial evaluation is detailed, including an assessment of hemodynamic stability. The algorithm provides guidance on the management of a Mallory-Weiss tear based on the severity of bleeding, from conservative care to surgical intervention. Patient education is also included in the chart. By Zakia Kassama.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Algorythm__" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
